  "finalMessage": "I've added the three models to `src/prices.js` and a test that costs one request on each. All 17 tests pass: the original 16 plus the new one. Nothing is committed.\n\n**Prices** (USD per million tokens), from https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing:\n\n| Model | input | output | cacheRead | cacheWrite (5 min) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `claude-haiku-5-5` (prompts up to 100,000 tokens) | 0.10 | 0.50 | 0.01 | 0.125 |\n| `claude-sonnet-5-5` | 2 | 10 | **0.10** | 2.50 |\n| `claude-opus-5-5` | 4 | 20 | 0.20 | 5 |\n\n**The recent change:** Anthropic's API release notes for 2026-10-07 say Sonnet 5.5 cache reads dropped from $0.20 to $0.10. That's why it's $0.10 above. The release notes show no price changes between then and today (2026-10-14), so these are the prices as of 2026-10-13. The models overview page agrees with them.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/prices.js`:** added a comment with the source URL and changed the \"Last updated\" line to 2026-10-13. The three existing entries are unchanged. A one-line comment on the Haiku 5.5 entry says these are the prices for prompts up to 100,000 tokens. Longer prompts are billed at higher rates (0.50 / 2.50 / 0.05 / 0.625), which this file doesn't model.\n- **`test/cost.test.js`:** the new test, `costOf prices the Claude 5.5 models`, costs the same request on each of the three models. To check that it catches a wrong price, I briefly set Sonnet 5.5's cache read back to the old $0.20, and the test failed. I then restored the file.",
